# Fork boundary

This repo is a fork of Hugging Face LeRobot. Custom behavior already lives in new modules. Do not grow the patch set on upstream files.

## Where new code goes

- Faults, recovery, and datagen: `src/lerobot/faults/`
- LIBERO scene changes: `src/lerobot/envs/libero_overlays/` (stock BDDL stays untouched)
- Tests for those features: `tests/faults/`, `tests/envs/test_libero_overlays.py`

Upstream plugin discovery only loads packages named `lerobot_robot_`, `lerobot_camera_`, `lerobot_teleoperator_`, `lerobot_policy_`, `lerobot_env_`, or `lerobot_strategy_`. A new file under `src/lerobot/faults/` is still inside this fork. It is the right place until that code moves to its own package.

## Do not extend these hooks

Fault flags and success-only recording belong on `lerobot-eval-faults` (`src/lerobot/faults/eval_cli.py`). Do not add them back to `EvalPipelineConfig` or `EvalConfig`.

These upstream files still carry a small seam. Do not add new fields or fork-only branches. Per-episode fields such as ``success`` are merged in ``src/lerobot/faults/episode_metadata.py`` around ``meta.save_episode``. Do not add ``episode_metadata`` back onto ``LeRobotDataset.save_episode``.

Overlays are ``--env.type=libero_overlay`` via ``lerobot-eval-overlay`` (``LiberoOverlayEnvConfig``). Do not put ``overlay`` back on stock ``LiberoEnv`` in ``configs.py`` or ``libero.py``. Headless rendering is ``install_headless_libero_renderer`` / ``OverlayLiberoEnv._ensure_env``, not a patch of stock ``_ensure_env`` in ``libero.py``.

- `src/lerobot/scripts/lerobot_eval.py` — `features_map` when recording eval episodes. Failure columns are off unless `annotate_failures=True`, which only `lerobot-eval-faults` sets.

```python
# Bad: another fork flag on the upstream eval config
class EvalPipelineConfig:
    fault: FaultInjectionConfig
    my_new_mode: bool = False

# Good: new fault behavior in src/lerobot/faults/, invoked by lerobot-eval-faults
```

Do not vendor a second LeRobot tree, and do not convert this repo into a submodule, to avoid editing those files. That does not remove the seam.
